<title>USA: Philippines buys 24,000 tonnes U.S. wheat - trade.</title>
<headline>Philippines buys 24,000 tonnes U.S. wheat - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines purchased approximately 24,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat early this week, exporters said.</p>
<p>The deal consisted of 18,000 tonnes of 14 percent protein Dark Northern Spring wheat off the west coast at about $192.00 a tonne, FOB, and 6,000 tonnes of Western White wheat at about $150 to $160 a tonne, FOB, one U.S. exporter said.</p>
<p>The exporter said shipments were slated for spot and first half April, out of Portland, Oregon.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
